# R2 startup successor: exact BootROM cause and bounded checks

The saved16KiB ROM has SHA-256 `ef07d54bdd259c7858483606118a3c704976801823c38ac5a2fcdffacd2d83fe`, CRC32 `0A428502`. Its watchdog function at0xA24 writes mask0x1FFFC to PSM.WDSEL at0x40010008. The actual PC_REBOOT command branch calls it at0x21FC; reset_usb_boot calls it at0x259E. CLOCKS and RESETS are selected for reset. SDK register definitions give PLL_USB CS reset1 (LOCK clear), PWR reset0x2D, and RTC clock CTRL0/DIV0x100.

The official [B2 ROM source](https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-bootrom-rp2040) explains the [watchdog reset](https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-bootrom-rp2040/blob/master/usb_device_tiny/runtime.c) and [ROM USB clock setup](https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-bootrom-rp2040/blob/master/bootrom/bootrom_main.c). ROM USB uses PLL_SYS at48MHz. The repository warns that its revision differs from the on-chip revision; the saved device bytes and their disassembly are the primary evidence here.

R1 required an already locked48MHz PLL_USB. Its failure at this post-ROM condition is reproduced by its real Thumb code. R2 initializes missing/invalid USB PLL only after declining an active RTC that depends on it. A valid existing PLL is retained. An explicit reset/unreset prevents SDK pll_init from returning early for a locked but bypassed PLL. No RTC mux/divider/reset or date setter is added. The accepted SET0 return remains a placeholder/fresh-base calendar with explicit clock HOLD.

The final linked image passes ten reset/clock cases, reproduces the parent failure, and rejects two separately mutated linked controls. Actual main runs up to its TinyUSB initialization call: ROM CRC, four mathematical ROM pointers, unchanged hot-code copying and identity globals are checked. Peripheral lock/readiness/mux/reset state is modeled explicitly. No USB initialization/enumeration, physical clock timing or performance is claimed from those models.

Only one final startup object differs;80 other SDK objects are reused unchanged. The mathematical blocks, their addresses, the complete fallback closure, dataset and72-state smoke plan are exact R1 bytes. Its274008 math-call evidence is inherited rather than rerun. The unsuccessful bypass trial is retained in `rejected-before-forced-PLL-reset/`; model-development failures (inconsistent ready/reset fixture, initially omitted SysTick and hot-copy write allowances) were corrected in the HOST harness, without changing mathematical code. Reported47 startup/parent calls and148 worker primitive calls count the completed final checks, not failed development attempts.

R1 payload/operator and committed checkpoint `fafce31ed` remain historical immutable packets. The separately bound operator successor and a fresh Root grant are required for any physical stage. M4, production sources, Git refs and device state were not modified during this successor work.
